# Defect 322, panel 197's R2, 2026-10-07: the debug word follows the level,
# `-g` at `-O0` and `-gline-tables-only` at `-O2` (`cli/flags.hero`,
# `debug_words`). What the line tables keep at every level is the location a
# sanitiser names: AddressSanitizer's report of a heap block read after it
# was freed carries this file's name and the line of the call below, at
# `--sanitize` (built at `-O2`, under line tables) and at `--sanitize -O0`
# (under `-g`), and it would carry neither under `-g0`, the word the sitting
# refused for it (measured by its ffi-pragmatist on this Mac and Linux, where
# `-g0` also named a false file). UBSan keeps its location under every word,
# so the witness is ASan's.
#
# The read is C's, in the header's `static inline`, compiled under the
# program's own words; its value is never used, so the plain runs print the
# same whatever the freed block holds.

extern "fixedbugs-322-a-sanitiser-names-the-hero-line-at-every-level.h"
    function read_after_free(v: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print("a freed block is read in C")
    print(read_after_free(v: 7))
